WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540
Deep inside each mitochondrion, the
inner membrane is folded into cristae.

2
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:09.370
Along it, the cell keeps pumping
protons out of the matrix,

3
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.080
across the membrane.

4
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.140
The membrane holds them back.

5
00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:18.240
So they pile up, until the space
beyond has a lower pH than the matrix.

6
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:24.030
So why would a cell pump protons uphill,
only to let them flood straight back?

7
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.790
In this mission, you'll follow electrons
as they are handed from carrier to carrier,

8
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.540
releasing energy at each transfer.

9
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.660
Then you'll see the final hand-off:
oxygen takes the electrons,

10
00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.410
and becomes water.

11
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.570
Your mission: explain why a
cell pumps protons uphill,

12
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.310
only to let them flood back.
